WEBVTT

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:17.900
Let's start with nothing at all. Just
linen... and a little light.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:27.071
Tonight we're painting two friends of
mine. They're a little strange.

00:00:27.071 --> 00:00:28.280
So are the best ones.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.890
Lead white. Every light we make starts
here.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:46.570
Yellow ochre. It's dirt, really. The best
colours are.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:55.070
Cadmium red. ...Home.

00:00:55.310 --> 00:00:58.090
Permanent alizarin. The crimson.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:04.313
HOLD IT! PERMANENT? That's not a colour,
folks, that's a PROMISE!

00:01:04.313 --> 00:01:08.080
And if you order in the next ten minutes—
BUT WAIT—

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:11.760
We don't wait here, friend... The paint's
open.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:13.250
...Understood.

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:21.150
Viridian. You'll never see it. It hides
inside our blacks.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:27.930
Prussian blue. A drop. Only ever a drop.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:33.470
And bone black. The night inside the coil.

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:40.110
FOURTEEN tubes! Most folks buy FORTY and
use SIX. The rest are in a drawer, CRYING.

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:47.990
And never more than three in a mix. Mix
everything, and you get brown.

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:59.450
Every brush says one thing. This is the
Broom. It says 'sky'.

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:03.490
The Pencil says 'an eye'.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.690
The Whisker says 'wire'.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:16.494
BUT HOLD ON— the KNIFE! It mixes! It
spreads! It SCULPTS!

00:02:16.494 --> 00:02:19.150
And it has NEVER needed a cord!

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:22.800
And the Rag. Light, taken back.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:29.170
...That one's mine. That one's not on the
roll.

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:40.610
Before colour, there's value. Squint, and
anything is a few lights and a few darks.

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:51.000
Colour is the clothes. Value is the bones.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:08.300
Imprimatura. A thin, warm tone first. Then
lift the light back out,

00:03:10.789 --> 00:03:13.740
while it's still open.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:21.102
Wet-in-wet. Tailor's Crimson, pulled
through wet white.

00:03:21.102 --> 00:03:24.420
The canvas does half the mixing.

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:36.010
Blending. The Cloud. Barely touch it...
like you're dusting a moth.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:51.000
Scumble. Over a dry dark, almost no paint
on the brush. Light through smoke.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:05.500
Over dry paint, a glaze is coloured glass.
Let the light in...

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:11.010
and ask it to come back a little redder.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:14.790
HE MADE IT LAST WEEK! That's TIME TRAVEL,
folks!

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:22.793
Hi— hey— is this live? I've been painting
along since the two a.m. one,

00:04:22.793 --> 00:04:28.168
only light on in my building, I'm on
canvas three. Quick question:

00:04:28.168 --> 00:04:30.530
is glazing the same as lying?

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:33.910
Hi, friend. It's more like whispering.

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:39.535
Whispering. Okay. Writing that on my hand.
It's for my sister, Rosie.

00:04:39.535 --> 00:04:46.035
She's nine today. She asked for the girl
with the tail. That was nineteen hours
ago.

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:48.650
Then we'll get her one with good teeth.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:58.620
Dry brush. Let the weave catch what the
brush won't give it.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:05.543
Let a PROFESSIONAL— IMPASTO, folks! LOOK
at that ridge!

00:05:05.543 --> 00:05:10.980
It'll still be there in a hundred years,
and I'm not even charging you for it!

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.740
Hehe.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:28.540
Lost and found. A hard edge says, look
here. A lost edge says, you already know.

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:47.530
Fat over lean. Each layer a little oilier
than the last, or it cracks...

00:05:48.204 --> 00:05:51.890
like a tight coat on a growing child.

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:58.510
Like a tight coat. Oh, that's sad. That's
beautiful and sad.

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:07.510
A fresh canvas. This one's for keeps...
Hold still, now.

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:13.880
We never start on white. White lies to you
about every value you put on it.

00:06:16.780 --> 00:06:22.764
When I was nineteen, I painted signs. A
farmer wanted FRESH EGGS,

00:06:22.764 --> 00:06:24.790
and a plain white egg.

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:32.320
Next morning, somebody'd given that egg a
crooked smile. I painted it out.

00:06:32.498 --> 00:06:37.190
Next morning, it was back. Bigger. So I
let it stay.

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:42.141
Twenty years later, the board's nailed to
a barn,

00:06:42.141 --> 00:06:46.430
and somebody's kept that smile going.
Wider every year.

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:53.936
You don't get to choose which part of your
work people keep.

00:06:53.936 --> 00:06:57.430
Usually it's the part you painted over.

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:03.901
You're not copying one big picture.

00:07:03.901 --> 00:07:07.350
You're copying a hundred and forty-four
little ones.

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:16.030
A hundred and forty-four. That's a gross.
That's literally a gross.

00:07:21.550 --> 00:07:23.680
Find the biggest movement first.

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:32.720
And under his dome, a real jaw. A person's
smile, stretched as far as it goes.

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:43.950
That's not a snake. That's her tail, and
it grows from her... as thick as she is.

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:51.170
The old picture tells three fibs. One
blade, eye at its root, plain handle.

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:57.570
C-four to E-six. You sank my battleship.

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:32.910
Find your lightest light first.

00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:38.590
Everything else is just a conversation
about how far away from it you are.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.780
...Hi.

00:08:55.990 --> 00:08:58.040
...Well. ...Hi there.

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:01.140
I liked the egg.

00:09:01.190 --> 00:09:02.190
...You heard that?

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:04.490
Hehe.

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:08.950
Is that— LITTLE LADY! Are you in the
MARKET for—

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:09.960
No.

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:12.490
Did— okay— did anybody else—

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:13.300
Mm-hm.

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:15.480
Okay. Okay. That's fine.

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:20.070
Every painting is three values pretending
to be a thousand.

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:25.760
THREE values! I've sold forty-piece sets
to men who needed THREE!

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:32.273
Squinting's not a technique, it's a
lifestyle. I've been squinting since
three.

00:09:32.273 --> 00:09:34.500
It's the coffee. And the cans.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.410
Have some water, friend.

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:42.082
Ah. I painted light around a blade that
isn't there any more.

00:09:42.082 --> 00:09:44.690
Painters call that a pentimento.

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:48.940
The picture got us started. It doesn't get
to finish.

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:51.110
Wait— can I still look at it?

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:54.970
No, friend. Neither can I.

00:10:00.742 --> 00:10:07.086
Hang on. Day one, six minutes in. Day two,
six forty-six. Day three, eight-twenty.

00:10:07.086 --> 00:10:12.348
That's a curve. That puts the last stroke
at exactly twenty minutes.

00:10:12.348 --> 00:10:14.217
Somebody owns a calendar.

00:10:14.267 --> 00:10:15.267
Hm.

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:19.690
Okay so— I've been up— doesn't matter how
long.

00:10:19.690 --> 00:10:26.190
There's a lamp in the lot outside my
window. Orange. The sodium kind. It hums.

00:10:26.672 --> 00:10:32.747
All night I'm looking at a red car, a red
mailbox, a red sign, and I'm thinking,

00:10:32.747 --> 00:10:35.632
that's a lot of red for a parking lot.

00:10:35.759 --> 00:10:41.323
Four-twelve, the sensor decides it's
morning. Click. Lamp's off.

00:10:41.323 --> 00:10:47.669
And the sky's that early blue, the blue
before blue... and nothing's red.

00:10:47.887 --> 00:10:54.011
The car's grey. The mailbox is grey. It
was never red. It was orange light,

00:10:54.011 --> 00:11:00.381
sitting on grey stuff. Except somebody's
brake lights, pulling out of the lot.

00:11:00.381 --> 00:11:02.177
Getting smaller. Gone.

00:11:02.539 --> 00:11:07.649
Red is the thing that's leaving. I've been
holding that since four-twelve.

00:11:07.649 --> 00:11:09.859
I needed to give it to somebody.

00:11:10.441 --> 00:11:16.361
Thank you for giving it to us. Under gold
light, red turns orange.

00:11:16.361 --> 00:11:19.501
Give it something cool to stand on.

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:23.120
There. That one's just for me.

00:11:30.990 --> 00:11:37.490
Coil Black. Alizarin, viridian, bone
black. Black with a heartbeat.

00:11:38.079 --> 00:11:43.249
We saved her a clean place. Drag a dark
through wet gold, and it's mud.

00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:48.459
Don't count the scales. Paint light on
six,

00:11:48.459 --> 00:11:51.730
and the eye paints the other nine hundred.

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:54.770
I count them.

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:58.410
Her tail grows from right here.

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:01.050
Heavier.

00:12:01.100 --> 00:12:02.100
...Heavier?

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:04.880
It weighs more than I do.

00:12:07.690 --> 00:12:08.690
Like this?

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:10.470
Heavier.

00:12:11.070 --> 00:12:14.370
...She's right. It's better.

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:26.318
This program is made possible by Wallpaper
Breaker:

00:12:26.318 --> 00:12:29.658
live wallpapers that get looked at before
they ship.

00:12:29.708 --> 00:12:35.287
By Wordhord, which keeps receipts on every
word you know. By Armies of Gielinor,

00:12:35.287 --> 00:12:37.630
back from a handful of screenshots.

00:12:37.680 --> 00:12:41.905
By Grind and Grimoire: a skateboarding
wizard with no poem written.

00:12:41.905 --> 00:12:45.860
By The Hidden Curriculum: everything
school forgot to teach you.

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:50.107
By BLACKWATER— ZOM— ...zombies. But you're
cave diving.

00:12:50.107 --> 00:12:52.181
...And by viewers like Aaron.

00:12:52.231 --> 00:12:57.843
He meant to draw HIM. He got me. In
Megabonk, I jump five point seven seven
metres.

00:12:57.893 --> 00:13:03.346
And the fighting game! Four hundred
matches, she won two hundred and four—

00:13:03.396 --> 00:13:05.450
He can't see the scoreboard.

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:10.960
Let's not talk for a while. Let's just
listen to it.

00:14:01.010 --> 00:14:03.290
...but wait... There's more.

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:05.020
...There always is.

00:14:06.090 --> 00:14:09.090
A cape is a flag that remembers the wind.

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:15.950
The old picture tore these capes to
confetti. A cape is one big shape.

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:21.825
Make mine flap more, Teacher. ...Please.

00:14:21.875 --> 00:14:23.545
A little more flap.

00:14:24.592 --> 00:14:28.773
Every time you tap the brush like that,
somebody at home sneezes.

00:14:28.823 --> 00:14:30.793
...Bless them.

00:14:31.242 --> 00:14:37.472
You sound closer. Do I sound closer? I
moved the phone. No I didn't. Did I?

00:14:37.825 --> 00:14:40.535
You're coming toward the light, Moth.

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:07.060
Does anybody else hear a bell? Every five
minutes. I've been counting. That's three.

00:15:07.398 --> 00:15:09.518
I think that's just the building.

00:15:09.976 --> 00:15:11.656
It's my house.

00:15:12.216 --> 00:15:14.046
...Then it's a lovely bell.

00:15:14.378 --> 00:15:17.478
Miss. ...My apologies for the noise.

00:15:17.654 --> 00:15:20.310
Accepted, Coupon.

00:15:20.360 --> 00:15:24.750
Wipe the brush almost dry. Let the weave
do the cotton.

00:15:25.720 --> 00:15:29.350
PRUSSIAN BLUE! ONE DROP, folks! It's
DENIM!

00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:38.993
Two turns. Not three. Three is GREEDY.

00:15:39.043 --> 00:15:45.163
Short pulls, folks! A knife runs dry fast,
so you RELOAD every time!

00:15:45.470 --> 00:15:50.290
Nothing's a mistake once you decide to
keep it. That one's hers now.

00:15:50.658 --> 00:15:53.640
Mine. ...Again.

00:15:53.690 --> 00:15:57.110
Ma'am, I can't. It's TWO turns.

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:05.420
Her sleeves are wool. Soft rolls. No
scales,

00:16:05.420 --> 00:16:08.810
or she'll look like she's made of snake.

00:16:09.081 --> 00:16:11.133
I'm not made of snake.

00:16:11.183 --> 00:16:13.563
No, young lady. You're not.

00:16:13.897 --> 00:16:19.987
Her mouth is one dark shape. Teeth go on
top, once it's dry.

00:16:21.090 --> 00:16:26.555
Here's the one time we wait on purpose. A
glaze needs a dry floor,

00:16:26.555 --> 00:16:28.790
and crimson takes its time.

00:16:31.100 --> 00:16:35.030
Sixty-six days? ...Wait. What day is it.

00:16:35.279 --> 00:16:41.609
Sixty-six days, in four easy payments.
That's not a price. That's a season.

00:16:41.722 --> 00:16:45.553
Say it loud, Coupon. I like it when you're
scared.

00:16:45.603 --> 00:16:47.223
...I'm not allowed.

00:16:57.540 --> 00:17:04.040
Metal is just a mirror. Don't paint metal.
Paint what it's looking at.

00:17:07.320 --> 00:17:13.820
Teeth are never white. White is for light.
One at a time, over the dry dark.

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:18.530
Wider.

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:20.090
...Perfect.

00:17:20.190 --> 00:17:23.540
That's how it feels from inside.

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:30.130
Leave that spot in her eye dry. White on
wet paint just disappears.

00:17:33.810 --> 00:17:38.820
A long, straight handle is the one place
I'll let you use a ruler. One pull.

00:17:41.890 --> 00:17:48.390
You fixed it. ...Nobody ever fixes
anything for me. ...I'll let you live.

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:55.519
Eleven years ago they gave me a brush to
sell. One sable hair.

00:17:55.519 --> 00:17:58.420
'For the thing you can almost see.'

00:17:58.634 --> 00:18:05.134
Four hundred airings. Loud, soft, once in
a hot tub. Not one order.

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:11.176
Airing four-oh-one, a lady called.
Seventy-nine. She'd painted her late
husband,

00:18:11.176 --> 00:18:13.070
and the eyelashes were wrong.

00:18:13.362 --> 00:18:18.080
I mailed it to her in a sock. A week
later, a letter. 'It worked.

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:19.822
Have you ever tried it?'

00:18:20.075 --> 00:18:26.575
I hadn't. Eleven years. Never once got it
wet. ...Chief? Can I do the wire?

00:18:28.797 --> 00:18:30.337
Go ahead, friend.

00:18:36.600 --> 00:18:39.108
Do you want to know why it's so heavy?

00:18:39.158 --> 00:18:40.678
Tell me after we finish.

00:18:40.763 --> 00:18:42.853
...Fine. After.

00:18:43.430 --> 00:18:46.710
The shadow of gold is a darker, cooler
gold.

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:54.503
Years back, a blind man came into my frame
shop. Mr. Hale. His dog, Captain,

00:18:54.503 --> 00:18:56.870
had died. He wanted a painting.

00:18:57.636 --> 00:19:01.181
I said, you won't be able to see it. He
said,

00:19:01.181 --> 00:19:05.356
'Then paint it so I can.' So I painted
Captain thick.

00:19:10.640 --> 00:19:17.140
He ran his fingers over it. 'You got his
left ear wrong.' There was a nick in it.

00:19:18.024 --> 00:19:20.850
I fixed it with my eyes closed.

00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:26.893
Paint for the hands, too. Our friend here
can't see.

00:19:26.893 --> 00:19:29.890
Let's give him something he can read.

00:19:37.590 --> 00:19:38.920
Twenty seconds.

00:19:41.340 --> 00:19:44.250
Would you? It's never been wet.

00:19:44.561 --> 00:19:46.511
...I think this one's hers.

00:19:50.480 --> 00:19:51.240
Eight.

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:53.350
Go ahead, Jefrie.

00:19:56.490 --> 00:19:57.290
Two.

00:19:58.790 --> 00:19:59.790
...There.

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:10.230
Mm. ...There she is.

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:12.370
There WE are.

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:29.990
Close your eyes, if you want.

00:20:30.430 --> 00:20:31.750
You can hear it.

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:47.100
It sounds like a road.

00:20:47.420 --> 00:20:50.400
A gravel road at night.

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:03.950
(giggles)

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:11.110
Conservators X-ray paintings because lead
white stops X-rays.

00:21:11.470 --> 00:21:12.930
You see where the white went...

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:15.920
so you see where the painter changed their
mind.

00:21:18.400 --> 00:21:22.660
And there's the light I painted round a
blade that isn't there any more.

00:21:28.250 --> 00:21:29.250
You found it.

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:31.660
I always put one in.

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:34.350
Usually it's the part you paint over.

00:21:34.450 --> 00:21:36.420
THERE'S A HOUSE IN IT.

00:21:36.470 --> 00:21:37.690
...Is anybody home?

00:21:40.270 --> 00:21:41.870
Hold still.

00:21:52.260 --> 00:21:53.260
...Hi.

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:03.550
That's not my tail.

00:22:03.700 --> 00:22:05.540
That's a stranger's snake.

00:22:05.700 --> 00:22:07.230
That's not my scythe.

00:22:07.490 --> 00:22:09.860
That's a can opener with ambitions.

00:22:13.120 --> 00:22:16.540
Theirs is confetti. Ours is a cape.

00:22:17.250 --> 00:22:18.720
Copy the shapes.

00:22:19.140 --> 00:22:20.650
Not the fibs.

00:22:22.230 --> 00:22:23.890
That's all of it.

00:22:23.940 --> 00:22:26.200
Every day at once.

00:22:26.730 --> 00:22:28.550
The middle's Tuesday.

00:22:29.050 --> 00:22:31.170
Like the rings in a tree.

00:22:31.480 --> 00:22:34.710
Ours just grew in a spiral.

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:37.000
Is he gone?

00:22:40.390 --> 00:22:41.190
Teacher.

00:22:41.240 --> 00:22:43.960
He looked at us for twenty minutes.

00:22:47.840 --> 00:22:48.840
Lucky.

00:22:49.580 --> 00:22:51.580
He gave you a person's mouth.

00:22:51.700 --> 00:22:54.020
Everybody always gives you a can.

00:23:00.340 --> 00:23:02.850
And my tail comes out of ME now.

00:23:02.950 --> 00:23:06.070
Before, it just sort of... hovered nearby.

00:23:06.190 --> 00:23:07.100
Like an uncle.

00:23:07.150 --> 00:23:10.540
Folks, I'd like to discuss an ENDORSEMENT—

00:23:11.170 --> 00:23:12.260
He says no.

00:23:12.310 --> 00:23:13.938
He says it nicely, though.

00:23:13.988 --> 00:23:16.203
Is the painting talking?

00:23:16.253 --> 00:23:17.895
Okay. That's fine.

00:23:17.945 --> 00:23:19.750
That's a normal amount of fine.

00:23:19.800 --> 00:23:20.800
(giggles)

00:23:25.480 --> 00:23:26.890
Are your blacks...

00:23:26.940 --> 00:23:27.540
DEAD?

00:23:27.590 --> 00:23:28.328
Flat?

00:23:28.378 --> 00:23:29.838
Do your shadows look like a HOLE...

00:23:29.888 --> 00:23:31.540
in your painting?

00:23:31.590 --> 00:23:33.897
Introducing COIL BLACK!

00:23:33.947 --> 00:23:37.348
Alizarin! Viridian! A HEAP of BONE!

00:23:37.398 --> 00:23:39.698
It's black with a HEARTBEAT!

00:23:41.500 --> 00:23:43.620
Operators are standing by!

00:23:44.797 --> 00:23:45.340
(giggles)

00:23:45.390 --> 00:23:46.125
...Ma'am.

00:23:46.175 --> 00:23:48.640
Not available in stores, because you MAKE
it.

00:23:48.690 --> 00:23:51.080
On your PALETTE. For FREE!

00:24:47.269 --> 00:24:49.369
FOURTEEN TUBES!

00:24:49.691 --> 00:24:51.201
ONE DROP!

00:24:52.161 --> 00:24:53.161
...sorry.

00:24:55.151 --> 00:24:57.081
ALL TOGETHER, FOLKS—

00:25:13.323 --> 00:25:14.753
STAYING!

00:25:18.181 --> 00:25:19.271
...knock on wood.

00:25:19.580 --> 00:25:20.580
Heavier.

00:26:21.000 --> 00:26:21.950
Only ever a drop of Prussian blue, I told
you.

00:26:22.000 --> 00:26:23.443
Let a PROFESSIONAL— S! O! L! D!

00:26:23.493 --> 00:26:24.450
Dots. Dots. Dots on dots. Okay— okay—

00:26:24.500 --> 00:26:25.500
Mine.

00:26:26.000 --> 00:26:26.440
Longer.

00:26:28.800 --> 00:26:29.590
Eyes.

00:26:29.640 --> 00:26:30.444
In every cage.

00:26:30.494 --> 00:26:31.120
NINETEEN NINETY-FIVE! A hundred years of
RIDGE, folks!

00:26:31.170 --> 00:26:32.830
They were always watching.

00:26:35.500 --> 00:26:37.350
And somewhere to come home to.

00:26:39.380 --> 00:26:40.860
...Hers is done.

00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:41.670
...There.

00:26:41.720 --> 00:26:43.840
Rosie's is done.

00:26:43.890 --> 00:26:45.620
...Great work, boss.

00:26:45.790 --> 00:26:46.900
Thank you, Coupon.

00:26:56.990 --> 00:26:59.296
Wherever you are tonight...

00:26:59.296 --> 00:27:04.590
I hope your paint stays wet exactly as
long as you need it to.

00:27:17.000 --> 00:27:18.130
BUT WAIT!

00:27:19.440 --> 00:27:20.580
...All right.

00:27:20.770 --> 00:27:21.770
One more.

00:27:40.980 --> 00:27:42.010
...Night, Moth.

00:27:51.500 --> 00:27:53.690
I'd pay anything for that.

00:28:00.442 --> 00:28:03.553
Number fourteen. Crimson Coil.

00:28:03.603 --> 00:28:04.990
Please don't touch.

00:28:05.040 --> 00:28:06.400
I can feel that.

00:28:07.450 --> 00:28:10.800
Lower the light, and every decision stands
up.

00:28:10.850 --> 00:28:14.010
That's mine. I signed it while you were
looking at the palette.

00:28:14.300 --> 00:28:17.000
This is how it was seen for most of
history.

00:28:17.050 --> 00:28:18.130
Keep this one.

00:28:18.550 --> 00:28:20.063
One colour of light.

00:28:20.113 --> 00:28:23.000
If the values are right, it still holds.

00:28:24.744 --> 00:28:27.794
Under ultraviolet, newer paint looks dark.

00:28:27.844 --> 00:28:29.480
That speck went in last.

00:28:29.530 --> 00:28:30.710
It did.

00:28:31.000 --> 00:28:32.850
...I look like somebody kept me.

00:28:36.500 --> 00:28:39.550
When I was small, the wind kept taking me.

00:28:40.600 --> 00:28:44.110
Every storm, the bell would ring... and
away I'd go.

00:28:45.200 --> 00:28:47.710
So I asked for something that's mine.

00:28:48.390 --> 00:28:50.830
Something that keeps me where I am.

00:28:50.990 --> 00:28:53.430
He gave me the heaviest thing he had.

00:28:54.500 --> 00:28:57.820
Now nothing carries me anywhere I don't
want to go.

00:28:58.220 --> 00:28:59.800
Everybody else leaves.

00:29:00.183 --> 00:29:02.413
Anyway.

00:29:06.000 --> 00:29:08.580
You've been watching for twenty-nine
minutes.

00:29:09.100 --> 00:29:10.920
You have a long-day face.

00:29:13.300 --> 00:29:15.870
You're not missing much. He's tired.

00:29:16.000 --> 00:29:18.400
There's a little me on your other screen.

00:29:19.200 --> 00:29:20.200
In the rain.

00:29:20.250 --> 00:29:21.090
I don't cook.

00:29:21.140 --> 00:29:22.493
I work the register.

00:29:22.543 --> 00:29:25.253
Go to bed. We'll still be here.

00:29:25.333 --> 00:29:26.800
We can't leave.

00:29:26.850 --> 00:29:27.880
Goodnight.

00:29:30.150 --> 00:29:30.560
Hi— hey— is this live?

00:29:30.610 --> 00:29:32.950
...Hi.

00:29:33.474 --> 00:29:36.324
FOURTEEN TUBES! FOURTEEN!

00:29:36.595 --> 00:29:38.255
WHAT TIME IS IT

00:29:40.200 --> 00:29:41.200
There.

00:29:41.500 --> 00:29:42.340
(giggles)

00:29:42.390 --> 00:29:43.200
HEAVIER! HEAVIER! HEAVIER!

00:29:43.250 --> 00:29:43.700
Hehe.

00:29:43.750 --> 00:29:44.200
Hehe.

00:29:44.250 --> 00:29:46.150
Hehe.

00:29:55.294 --> 00:29:58.154
Mix everything, and you get brown.

00:29:59.000 --> 00:29:59.450
Again.

